  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Baboon** (1 review): Reviewer says Baboon is a poor fit for a date mixtape of the love songs [2]\n- **Tollund Man** (1 other source): Tollund Man opened the encore, followed by The Best Ever Death Metal Band in Denton [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Hot Garden Stomp**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **You're in Maya**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n- **Pure Gold**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: International Small Arms Traffic Blues [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **08InternationalSmallArmsTraffic** (recommended): source not stated; 13 songs; 53 min; rated 4/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer finds the recording well made [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Set opened with There Will Be No Divorce and Jenny, then 02-75 came after Minnesota, none of which are in the setlist [1]\n- There is little stage banter between songs on this recording [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **08InternationalSmallArmsTraffic**: Taped with a handheld analog tape recorder [1]",
